<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    A tree (RimWorld: Plant_TreePoplar, from Plants_Wild_Temperate). Its own file, additively.

    WHY IT EXISTS. Every building the settlement decides it needs costs wood (Buildings_Structural.xml), and
    before this file nothing on a generated map could ever produce any. WoodLog's own description said "harvested
    from a tree", and there was no tree. The only wood a map ever held was the odd stack of ruin loot
    (MapGen.GenStep_Ruins), so a founding band placed a bed blueprint for every citizen and then waited for
    materials that could not exist: seed 777 of the storyteller bench had no wood on its map at all and built
    no bed in 45 days.

    ONE SPECIES. RimWorld scatters a biome's own trees (oak and poplar in a temperate forest, pine in a boreal
    one, teak in a jungle). This port has one generic undergrowth marker (Plants_Wild.xml) rather than per-biome
    plant lists, so it gets one tree to match, placed at the density the tile's Timber deposit promises
    (MapGen.GenStep_Trees). Poplar is the one RimWorld grows in the most biomes (temperate forest, boreal
    forest and grassland).

    THE NUMBERS are RimWorld's, from the wiki's poplar page: harvest yield 27 wood, 15.05 days to grow, path
    cost 42, pass-through-only, 200 hit points, 80% flammability, 25% cover. harvestMinGrowth 0.4 is the wiki's
    trees page ("at 40% growth, it is possible to obtain 50% of their yield"); this port's Plant.Harvest scales
    yield linearly with growth, so a 40% tree gives 40% rather than 50%, the deviation Plant.Harvest already
    records. Cutting takes JobDriver_PlantWork.CutWorkAmount, not RimWorld's 800 ticks, because this port's
    PlantProperties carries no per-species harvestWork.
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Plant_TreePoplar</defName>
    <label>poplar tree</label>
    <description>A fast-growing tree with pale bark. Felled, it gives good straight wood.</description>
    <category>Plant</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Plant</thingClass>
    <tickerType>Long</tickerType>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>42</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.25</fillPercent>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <destroyable>true</destroyable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>200</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0.8</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <growDays>15.05</growDays>
      <harvestedThingDef>WoodLog</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>27</harvestYield>
      <harvestMinGrowth>0.4</harvestMinGrowth>
      <harvestTag>Wood</harvestTag>
      <!-- RimWorld's TreeBase sets this: a roof cannot go up over a standing tree, so a builder fells it
           first (Building.RoofUtility.FirstBlockingThing / HandleBlockingThingJob). -->
      <interferesWithRoof>true</interferesWithRoof>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
